91
00:05:30,205 --> 00:05:31,206
Hmm...

92
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:33,083
Shit.

93
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:34,709
[sighs]

94
00:05:40,924 --> 00:05:44,594
[vocalizing]

95
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:48,181
-Bang!
-Jeez!

96
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:55,564
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music fades]

97
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:59,150
NORTH MEXICO AERONAUTICAL CENTER

98
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,322
[sighs contentedly]

99
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:15,834
[in Spanish] That was
an impressive operation, Flex Cop.

100
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:17,794
[in Spanish] Thank you very much.

101
00:06:21,756 --> 00:06:23,800
[narrator, in Korean]
Next week's Specialist

102
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:26,595
is a third-generation billionaire heir
and violent crimes detective,

103
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:28,680
Senior Inspector Jin Isoo.

104
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:32,225
He recently arrested members
of a pyramid scheme ring in Mexico.

105
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:36,354
Detective Jin joined the police through
a special recruitment program for lawyers

106
00:06:36,438 --> 00:06:38,273
and has since built an impressive career.

107
00:06:39,316 --> 00:06:42,027
He uncovered the dark secrets
of a powerful business family,

108
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:44,362
solved the murder case
of artist Noh Youngjae,

109
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:48,825
and held an exhibition for the painter
who died after being gravely wronged.

110
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:53,747
He caught the killers
who preyed on the elderly

111
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:57,000
and retrieved the long-lost national seal,
which he donated to the state.

112
00:06:57,083 --> 00:07:02,047
Don't miss next week's episode
on Flex Cop Senior Inspector Jin Isoo.

113
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:05,216
SPECIALIST
FLEX X COP SENIOR INSPECTOR JIN ISOO

114
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:08,219
NUMBER 1 SAFETY!! NUMBER 1 PUBLIC ORDER!!
GANGHA POLICE STATION

115
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:09,554
[tires screech]

116
00:07:09,638 --> 00:07:12,182
[engine roaring]

117
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:23,151
[♪ upbeat music playing]

118
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:27,197
Ah. You're here early. Hello.

119
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,157
-The weather's lovely today--
-[director] Cut.

120
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,241
KANG JAEEUN - JANG HYEONWOO

121
00:07:30,325 --> 00:07:31,618
You don't need to say hello.

122
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:34,412
Just do what you'd normally do.

123
00:07:34,496 --> 00:07:35,497
Let's try that again.

124
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,999
-[camera lens whirs]
-Got it.

125
00:07:38,083 --> 00:07:40,585
-We're going again.
-[car door closes]

126
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:44,005
[camera lens whirs]

127
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:51,346
All right, come on in.

128
00:07:51,429 --> 00:07:55,266
Ah, the best veteran detective
of the Violent Crime Investigation Team 1

129
00:07:55,350 --> 00:07:58,186
and my right-hand man,
Inspector Park Junyoung.

130
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,482
VIOLENT CRIME INVESTIGATION TEAM 1
INSPECTOR PARK JUNYOUNG

131
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:05,068
The golden rookie of Team 1
and my left-hand man,

132
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:06,569
Senior Police Officer Choi Kyungjin.

133
00:08:06,653 --> 00:08:07,987
[clears throat] Hello.

134
00:08:08,071 --> 00:08:09,864
SENIOR POLICE OFFICER CHOI KYUNGJIN

135
00:08:11,825 --> 00:08:13,451
Huh? Dr. Yoon?

136
00:08:14,369 --> 00:08:15,537
Come in.

137
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:18,832
And that is

138
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:22,335
the NFS's best forensic pathologist,
Dr. Yoon Jiwon.

139
00:08:22,419 --> 00:08:24,129
NFS FORENSIC PATHOLOGIST
DR. YOON JIWON

140
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:25,588
Why is she here?

141
00:08:25,672 --> 00:08:27,924
Go ahead. You can pass through.

142
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:29,801
I think she came on purpose.

143
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:34,514
-This is Violent Crime...
-Ah!

144
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:37,517
These well-dressed folks here
are Violent Crime Investigation Team 2.

145
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,935
[chuckles]

146
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:40,478
-Got a wedding to go to?
-No, no.

147
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:41,604
[both chuckle]

148
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:44,733
VIOLENT CRIME INVESTIGATION TEAM 2

149
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:46,651
[Isoo] Now, don't block the camera.
Move aside.

150
00:08:46,735 --> 00:08:48,820
Move aside. Huh. Oh.

151
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:52,073
That's our team leader's desk.

152
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:55,243
She went to LA on a training program.

153
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,245
I don't know who our new leader will be,

154
00:08:57,328 --> 00:09:00,290
but I'm here waiting for you,
so please come join us.

155
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:01,791
My desk is over there.

156
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:03,793
[sighs contentedly]

157
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:06,963
Oh, this. As you know,
I joined through the lawyer track.

158
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:10,717
So I went to the police academy
and graduated top of my class again.

159
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,595
I just don't seem to know
how to be average. Huh.

160
00:09:14,179 --> 00:09:15,180
And this.

161
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:18,183
[sighs contentedly] I made this

162
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:20,101
so that anyone can report anything,

163
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:22,103
and no crime goes undetected.

164
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:24,814
But nothing big has been reported so far.

165
00:09:24,898 --> 00:09:26,316
Just missing dog reports.

166
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,609
What am I, John Wick?

167
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:29,152
MESSAGES

168
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:32,030
Oh, this one looks interesting.

169
00:09:32,614 --> 00:09:33,615
Let's see.

170
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:37,202
[distorted voice] Detective Jin.
Let the game begin.

171
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:38,411
What's this?

172
00:09:38,495 --> 00:09:40,121
[computer chimes]

173
00:09:40,205 --> 00:09:42,540
-I have a gift for you.
-Huh?

174
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:56,846
This looks suspicious.

175
00:09:57,722 --> 00:09:58,807
Right?

176
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:00,475
Detective Park, come see this.

177
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:06,231
What is it this time?

178
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:13,905
Oh. This is Hansu Department Store.

179
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:16,032
It's ours?

180
00:10:16,116 --> 00:10:18,827
Yes, I saw that
when I went there with my girlfriend.

181
00:10:18,910 --> 00:10:20,078
It might be another prank.

182
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,997
Right.

183
00:10:23,081 --> 00:10:25,166
People send all kinds of messages here.

184
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:27,127
Let's go check it out.

185
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,381
It's not like we have
any usable footage right now.

186
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:33,466
Then, shall we? Huh?

187
00:10:34,134 --> 00:10:35,135
Let's move out!

188
00:10:35,218 --> 00:10:38,096
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

189
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:40,640
-Come on.
-Let's move out! Mmm!

190
00:10:44,978 --> 00:10:46,020
[sighs]

191
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:49,941
Looks like we've got ourselves
a most interesting case.

192
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,609
Detective Park, you drive.

193
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,532
Cut. We're moving out too.

194
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:58,783
Let's move out.

195
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:01,828
[music increases in tempo]

196
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:11,462
[excited chatter]

197
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:19,262
-Bro, this is it.
-[Isoo] Huh.

198
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:21,014
Yeah? Give it here, Detective Choi.

199
00:11:23,266 --> 00:11:25,059
I don't get what we're doing here.

200
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:26,644
They're filming.

201
00:11:26,728 --> 00:11:28,771
[♪ tense music playing]

202
00:11:29,731 --> 00:11:30,899
[sighs]

203
00:11:33,193 --> 00:11:34,611
[cell phone vibrating]

204
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:36,487
Hey.

205
00:11:40,283 --> 00:11:41,784
[distorted voice] You found it quickly.

206
00:11:41,868 --> 00:11:43,995
Are we being watched right now?

207
00:11:48,041 --> 00:11:49,375
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[in English] Hint.

208
00:11:49,459 --> 00:11:50,501
Hmm...

209
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:53,880
[cell phone vibrating]

210
00:11:55,215 --> 00:11:56,591
[in Korean] A priest.

211
00:11:56,674 --> 00:11:59,344
A box, hash D... What is this?

212
00:11:59,928 --> 00:12:01,054
It's a Hex color code.

213
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:02,513
Tan.

214
00:12:02,597 --> 00:12:04,140
TAN

215
00:12:04,766 --> 00:12:06,309
I have a bad feeling about this.

216
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:08,144
[♪ tense music continues]

217
00:12:21,950 --> 00:12:23,952
[Junyoung] What goes inside
the parentheses?

218
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:25,536
Width?

219
00:12:26,037 --> 00:12:27,038
Or height?

220
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:28,623
Tan color. Tan.

221
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,250
Hey.

222
00:12:34,337 --> 00:12:36,965
[inhales sharply] I think it's this.

223
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:41,469
Width, height, or...

224
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:42,637
Breadth?

225
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:44,597
Bomb?

226
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:47,892
Homemade.

227
00:12:49,769 --> 00:12:51,020
-Homemade bomb.
-Homemade bomb.

228
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:53,022
Don't touch that!

229
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:55,024
-[clicks]
-[beeping]

230
00:12:55,108 --> 00:12:56,651
-[Kyungjin] Bro!
-What?

231
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:57,777
Don't move. Stay still.

232
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:59,070
[Isoo] Why? What is it?

233
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,405
Just hold still.

234
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:02,323
Why? What's wrong?

235
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:03,616
I told you not to touch it.

236
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:08,037
[beeping continues]

237
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:11,624
This is a bomb.

238
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:14,669
You should've told me sooner!

239
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:17,422
Zoom in.

240
00:13:17,505 --> 00:13:18,840
[softly] What do I do?

241
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:20,008
Stop filming.

242
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,635
God, what do I do?

243
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:26,597
[alarm ringing]

244
00:13:26,681 --> 00:13:28,933
[PA announcement] A security threat
has been detected in the building.

245
00:13:29,017 --> 00:13:32,437
All customers,
please evacuate immediately.

246
00:13:35,023 --> 00:13:36,441
[officer] Slowly, please!

247
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:38,568
To the left, please.

248
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,236
As fast as you safely can.

249
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,946
Please exit in an orderly manner.

250
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:44,532
[PA announcement] A security threat
has been detected in the building.

251
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:47,869
All customers,
please evacuate immediately.

252
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:51,539
Shouldn't we be leaving too?

253
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:53,666
It's not safe, so you guys should go too.

254
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:56,169
Okay. Let's pack it up.

255
00:13:56,252 --> 00:13:58,046
[nervously] Pack it up.

256
00:13:58,129 --> 00:13:59,130
[Jaeeun] Quickly.

257
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:01,257
[Isoo grunts]

258
00:14:02,008 --> 00:14:03,092
[line ringing]

259
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:04,594
Chief.

260
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:07,096
Please send in the bomb squad.

261
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:09,640
Yes. Okay.

262
00:14:09,724 --> 00:14:11,434
[grunts in frustration]

263
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,102
Bro, don't worry.

264
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:14,479
The bomb squad's on the way.

265
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:15,980
That's not it.

266
00:14:16,481 --> 00:14:18,149
-My leg's killing me.
-Your leg?

267
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:19,734
Let me massage it.

268
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:21,986
-No, the right leg.
-The other one.

269
00:14:22,487 --> 00:14:23,905
Here? Down below?

270
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:25,073
-Now, the left.
-The left.

271
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,492
-[Kyungjin] Down below?
-[Isoo] Yeah, down below.

272
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:28,576
[inhales sharply]

273
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:30,870
[Jaeeun] Do you have a clear shot?

274
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:32,622
Yes, a really clear shot.

275
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,999
Shouldn't we be evacuating?

276
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,752
You want to pass up
an opportunity like this?

277
00:14:37,835 --> 00:14:39,712
Some people even go into war zones.

278
00:14:39,796 --> 00:14:41,297
Get your act together.

279
00:14:42,924 --> 00:14:44,884
[police sirens approaching]

280
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:53,726
SPECIAL OPERATIONS UNIT

281
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:00,566
This way.

282
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,987
-It's right here.
-[Isoo] Over here.

283
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:06,447
[SOU lead] Step back.

284
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,910
Run an X-ray.

285
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,411
Don't move if you want to live.

286
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:17,500
DANGER

287
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:28,594
[device rapidly beeping]

288
00:15:28,678 --> 00:15:30,096
[grunts softly]

289
00:15:34,183 --> 00:15:35,226
[digital beep]

290
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:36,352
[SOU lead] Explosive confirmed.

291
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:38,521
There's a pressure plate under the device.

292
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:39,647
We'll disarm it here.

293
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,066
[♪ tense music playing]

294
00:15:50,241 --> 00:15:51,576
Shh... [groans nervously]

295
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:54,328
What do I do? How do we...

296
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,224
[♪ suspenseful music intensifies]

297
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,274
Is it done?

298
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,359
-Is it done?
-No.

299
00:16:25,443 --> 00:16:26,777
It'll detonate in 10 seconds.

300
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:28,821
Huh?

301
00:16:28,905 --> 00:16:30,823
[SOU lead] On three,
run back as fast as you can.

302
00:16:30,907 --> 00:16:32,074
-What?
-[SOU lead] Three.

303
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:33,326
-Can I let go?
-[SOU lead] Two.

304
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:34,785
-Bro.
-Do I let go?

305
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:36,495
-[SOU lead] One.
-Bro, run!

306
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:39,457
[panting]

307
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:40,791
[SOU lead chuckling]

308
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:45,087
Why didn't it go off?

309
00:16:46,714 --> 00:16:48,257
[SOU lead] Device rendered safe.

310
00:16:55,181 --> 00:16:56,349
Hey, nutjob.

311
00:16:58,226 --> 00:16:59,685
I told you to stay out of trouble.

312
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:10,071
[♪ upbeat music playing]

313
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:11,948
-Instructor Joo Hyera?
-[chuckles]

314
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:14,325
NATIONAL POLICE COUNTERTERRORISM TEAM
TEAM LEADER JOO HYERA

315
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:16,619
[exhales sharply]

316
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:19,205
[♪ upbeat music playing]

317
00:17:24,794 --> 00:17:26,295
[upbeat music stops]

318
00:17:26,379 --> 00:17:28,047
[Hyera] Did someone kill your dog?

319
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,507
You think you're John Wick?

320
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:30,675
Are you Keanu Reeves?

321
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:31,842
I was just...

322
00:17:31,926 --> 00:17:33,261
[Hyera] Listen up.

323
00:17:36,514 --> 00:17:39,725
You are issued firearms
to protect the public.

324
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:42,979
Use it only as a last resort,
and use it as safely as possible.

325
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:45,773
We just have to hit the target, don't we?

326
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:48,943
So you're the nutjob of this class.

327
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:50,236
[exhales softly]

328
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:55,241
[target pulley whirring]

329
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:56,659
[Isoo sighs]

330
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:59,412
[in English] My name is John Wick.

331
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:00,746
[sighs contentedly]

332
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:03,416
[in Korean] Looks like
a civilian passing by got hit.

333
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:05,376
-What are you going to do about it?
-Huh?

334
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:08,796
[Hyera] Eyes forward.

335
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:10,047
[groans]

336
00:18:10,131 --> 00:18:11,757
[♪ upbeat music playing]

337
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:18,472
-Stand straight.
-[sighs softly]

338
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:21,392
Both hands on the gun.

339
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:27,356
Go sit down.

340
00:18:27,982 --> 00:18:28,983
[sighs]

341
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:31,110
Shall we try someone tall this time?

342
00:18:31,193 --> 00:18:32,236
Any volunteers?

343
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,696
I'll do it.

344
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:36,532
[recruits] Ooh!

345
00:18:36,616 --> 00:18:37,658
Jin Isoo, come on up.

346
00:18:40,328 --> 00:18:42,580
-Let's do this!
-[recruits cheering]

347
00:18:48,169 --> 00:18:49,795
Don't come crying even if you get hurt.

348
00:18:49,879 --> 00:18:50,880
All right. Come at me.

349
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,006
[yells]

350
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,217
Oh.

351
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,185
[groans]

352
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:05,770
You're not crying, are you?

353
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:06,896
[exhales sharply]

354
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:09,982
[training officer] You're doing great.
You're almost there.

355
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,028
Hey, nutjob!

356
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,821
You're abandoning your teammates?

357
00:19:15,905 --> 00:19:16,906
[whistle blows]

358
00:19:21,077 --> 00:19:23,162
-Defensive position!
-[recruits] Defensive position!

359
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:25,623
Advance!

360
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:28,376
[grunting]

361
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:34,173
[exclaims]

362
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:36,884
[grunts]

363
00:19:37,385 --> 00:19:39,345
-[engine revs]
-[tires screeching]

364
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:45,893
[tires screeching]

365
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,734
Hey, nutjob!

366
00:19:53,818 --> 00:19:55,027
[tires screech]

367
00:19:58,155 --> 00:19:59,323
Back to start!

368
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:04,787
-[whistle blows]
-[Isoo] Seven, eight, nine.

369
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:05,871
[whistle blows]

370
00:20:06,789 --> 00:20:07,998
[whistle blows]

371
00:20:08,874 --> 00:20:10,751
Hey, nutjob. Do it properly.

372
00:20:13,337 --> 00:20:15,423
-Jeez, I lost count.
-[whistle blows]

373
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:17,258
[whistle blows rhythmically]

374
00:20:20,678 --> 00:20:21,846
[whistle echoes]

375
00:20:23,973 --> 00:20:25,182
[Isoo] That instructor from hell...

376
00:20:25,266 --> 00:20:26,517
It's her?

377
00:20:27,101 --> 00:20:28,644
But she's with Counterterrorism.

378
00:20:29,812 --> 00:20:32,314
She was filling in
for an instructor on sick leave.

379
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,733
She hates me.

380
00:20:34,984 --> 00:20:36,193
[sighs wearily]

381
00:20:36,277 --> 00:20:38,112
God, the trauma. [sighs]

382
00:20:41,532 --> 00:20:42,616
[sighs]

383
00:20:46,537 --> 00:20:47,580
SPECIALIST

384
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:50,040
-[Isoo] My leg's killing me.
-[Kyungjin] Your leg? Let me massage it.

385
00:20:50,124 --> 00:20:51,542
-[Isoo] No, the right leg.
-[Kyungjin] The other one.

386
00:20:51,625 --> 00:20:52,793
[grunts on screen]

387
00:20:52,877 --> 00:20:54,086
-[Kyungjin] Here? Down below?
-[Isoo] Now, the left.

388
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:55,171
[Kyungjin] The left.

389
00:20:55,713 --> 00:20:57,256
-[Kyungjin] Down below?
-[Isoo] Yeah, down below.

390
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:59,175
We can't use this clip of Jin Isoo.

391
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:00,509
He looks like an idiot.

392
00:21:01,469 --> 00:21:03,471
-Then what do we do?
-[keyboard clacks]

393
00:21:03,554 --> 00:21:04,555
[sighs in exasperation]

394
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,766
But this is such a great story.

395
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:09,518
[keyboard clacks]

396
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:13,022
[♪ quirky music playing]

397
00:21:13,105 --> 00:21:14,231
[keyboard clacks]

398
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:18,903
Hey.

399
00:21:18,986 --> 00:21:21,447
Send the footage of Jin Isoo
to the news team.

400
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:23,032
But what about our story?

401
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:24,366
[keyboard clacks]

402
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:30,164
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

403
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:32,041
[news anchor 1] Earlier today,
a homemade bomb was discovered

404
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:33,709
at Hansu Department Store.

405
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:36,629
The billionaire heir
and detective of Gangha Police Station,

406
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:39,298
Detective Jin Isoo,
discovered the explosive.

407
00:21:39,381 --> 00:21:42,468
[news anchor 2] He seems frozen
in the footage. What transpired?

408
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:45,221
[news anchor 1] Detective Jin didn't know
it was a bomb

409
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:46,555
and triggered it by accident.

410
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:49,767
[news anchor 2] And why is he reacting
like that? The bomb didn't even go off.

411
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,227
If you look at the footage--

412
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:52,478
[sighs in exasperation]

413
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:55,397
-Chief Park.
-Yes, sir.

414
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:58,526
I didn't want to come here.

415
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:02,196
Because of Jin Isoo.

416
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:04,990
If I'd had another option,
I wouldn't be here.

417
00:22:05,074 --> 00:22:06,158
Yes, sir.

418
00:22:06,242 --> 00:22:08,369
The head of the police station retired,

419
00:22:08,452 --> 00:22:10,079
and his team leader went abroad,

420
00:22:10,663 --> 00:22:13,082
so what is he still doing here?

421
00:22:13,165 --> 00:22:14,166
He's a chaebol heir.

422
00:22:14,250 --> 00:22:16,627
He should be running the company
or off somewhere enjoying himself.

423
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:18,295
So why?

424
00:22:18,379 --> 00:22:19,547
Because he's a detective.

425
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:24,760
I hate to admit it,
but Jin Isoo is a good detective.

426
00:22:24,844 --> 00:22:27,513
Right, he's a good detective,

427
00:22:27,596 --> 00:22:30,432
so he's earned himself
two excessive force complaints

428
00:22:30,516 --> 00:22:32,184
and three civil lawsuits.

429
00:22:32,268 --> 00:22:35,062
[chuckles] These were all cleared, sir.

430
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:36,272
Chief Park.

431
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:39,149
Come to your senses.

432
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:44,738
He's nothing but trouble for our station.

433
00:22:45,573 --> 00:22:48,659
I've been here less than a month,
and he's already screwed up.

434
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:49,910
What are you going to do?

435
00:22:49,994 --> 00:22:52,913
The Counterterrorism Team
will assess the bomb

436
00:22:52,997 --> 00:22:54,999
and work with
the Violent Crime Investigation Team 1.

437
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:57,459
The Cybercrime Team
is tracking down who sent the DM.

438
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,212
[sighs] God, I...

439
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:04,425
Why haven't you found them
a new team leader?

440
00:23:05,009 --> 00:23:07,303
Because no one wants the job.

441
00:23:07,386 --> 00:23:08,804
See?

442
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:11,765
Who'd want to manage
a rich kid who was handed the job?

443
00:23:11,849 --> 00:23:13,017
Huh?

444
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:15,102
I'll keep looking, sir.

445
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:18,022
Just focus on the investigation.

446
00:23:18,105 --> 00:23:19,189
Go catch the guy!

447
00:23:19,273 --> 00:23:21,775
Yes, sir.

448
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:24,320
[sighs in exasperation]

449
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:27,323
[news anchor 1] Earlier today,
a homemade bomb was discovered

450
00:23:27,406 --> 00:23:28,866
at Hansu Department Store.

451
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:32,036
The billionaire heir
and detective of Gangha Police Station,

452
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:33,662
Detective Jin Isoo,
discovered the explosive...

453
00:23:33,746 --> 00:23:35,164
[groans] My leg's numb.

454
00:23:35,915 --> 00:23:37,207
I can't bear it anymore!

455
00:23:37,917 --> 00:23:39,209
You can't.

456
00:23:39,293 --> 00:23:41,003
It'll go off if you move!

457
00:23:41,754 --> 00:23:43,213
[news anchor 2] And why is he
reacting like that?

458
00:23:43,297 --> 00:23:44,423
The bomb didn't even go off.

459
00:23:44,506 --> 00:23:45,507
-Three minutes.
-Thanks.

460
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,009
[Byungsik, in English] Okay.

461
00:23:48,385 --> 00:23:50,721
[in Korean] Turn the TV off!
We're on duty.

462
00:23:51,722 --> 00:23:53,182
-That's not funny.
-Bro!

463
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:55,976
VIOLENT CRIME INVESTIGATION TEAM 1
PARK JUNYOUNG

464
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:57,770
I told you not to make fun of him.

465
00:23:57,853 --> 00:23:59,313
[chuckles softly]

466
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:01,774
How could I not? It's too entertaining.

467
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:03,192
This one's good for 10 years.

468
00:24:11,784 --> 00:24:13,494
MR. CHOI
INCOMING CALL

469
00:24:13,577 --> 00:24:15,496
[cell phone ringing through car audio]

470
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:18,082
Hi, Mr. Choi.

471
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:19,166
Detective Jin.

472
00:24:20,084 --> 00:24:22,211
What happened? Are you all right?

473
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:25,089
I'm not all right.
I'm so embarrassed I could die.

474
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:26,256
[sighs]

475
00:24:26,632 --> 00:24:27,925
As long as you weren't hurt.

476
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:30,219
There's nothing wrong
with being embarrassed.

477
00:24:35,557 --> 00:24:36,934
[Isoo sighs]

478
00:24:37,393 --> 00:24:38,602
You're the great Jin Isoo.

479
00:24:38,686 --> 00:24:40,479
Are you really going to let this
get to you?

480
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:42,690
He's right, bro. Cheer up.

481
00:24:42,773 --> 00:24:44,900
You guys didn't make the news.

482
00:24:44,984 --> 00:24:47,611
The most humiliating moment
of my life is on TV right now.

483
00:24:47,695 --> 00:24:49,780
Come on, bro. People will forget about it.

484
00:24:49,863 --> 00:24:52,032
Forget? They won't forget.

485
00:24:52,116 --> 00:24:53,117
This'll last a decade.

486
00:24:56,704 --> 00:25:01,000
Then again, your ex slapping you
on Gangnam-daero was four years ago.

487
00:25:01,083 --> 00:25:02,668
Is that still going around?

488
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:04,586
Then this might last forever.

489
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:05,671
[gasps]

490
00:25:07,089 --> 00:25:09,383
You should just carve it
into your tombstone.

491
00:25:09,466 --> 00:25:11,093
"The man who triggered a bomb."

492
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:12,344
[laughing]

493
00:25:14,847 --> 00:25:15,848
Bro.

494
00:25:18,058 --> 00:25:19,560
-Hey, where are you going?
-Bro.

495
00:25:19,643 --> 00:25:20,894
-Hey, Bomb Guy.
-Bro!

496
00:25:20,978 --> 00:25:22,104
[Junyoung] Wait up!

497
00:25:22,730 --> 00:25:23,814
Bomb Guy.

498
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:25,691
-Come on.
-Bro.

499
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,694
How many times is this now?

500
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:30,487
-Also...
-You're laughing?

501
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:33,198
You're seriously laughing right now?

502
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:35,701
Sorry.

503
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:39,413
The news team kept begging us,
saying it was a huge scoop.

504
00:25:40,122 --> 00:25:41,206
-Sorry.
-Sorry.

505
00:25:41,749 --> 00:25:44,293
Even so, you made me look
like a complete idiot.

506
00:25:44,376 --> 00:25:45,669
In that kind of situation,

507
00:25:45,753 --> 00:25:48,213
anyone would have looked like an idiot.

508
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:52,760
Are you mocking me right now?

509
00:25:52,843 --> 00:25:55,054
Or are you trying to rub it in?
Which is it?

510
00:25:57,973 --> 00:25:58,974
She's coming. Let's go.

511
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:02,519
[♪ dramatic music playing]

512
00:26:16,116 --> 00:26:17,576
They've moved on to her, haven't they?

513
00:26:18,577 --> 00:26:20,579
Well, she is pretty cool.

514
00:26:20,662 --> 00:26:21,830
I'm a fan too now.

515
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:24,166
Are you moving on to her too?

516
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:25,584
-We'll see.
-"We'll see"?

517
00:26:25,667 --> 00:26:26,835
"We'll see"?

518
00:26:26,919 --> 00:26:27,920
That little...

519
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:30,422
Hang in there, nutjob.

520
00:26:31,006 --> 00:26:32,007
What the...

521
00:26:34,176 --> 00:26:35,385
This is ridiculous.

522
00:26:35,469 --> 00:26:37,387
Ugh. My head hurts.

523
00:26:37,471 --> 00:26:38,472
Jeez.

524
00:26:39,223 --> 00:26:40,224
[sighs]

525
00:26:40,307 --> 00:26:41,975
[♪ quirky music playing]

526
00:26:42,059 --> 00:26:43,477
PRIEST, BREADTH, TAN (HEX CODE)

527
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:44,812
PHOTO EVIDENCE 3, BOMB X-RAY

528
00:26:44,895 --> 00:26:46,772
HANSU DEPARTMENT STORE
ATTEMPTED BOMBING

529
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:50,150
The bomb appears to have been made
with ammonium nitrate.

530
00:26:50,234 --> 00:26:51,610
It's a simple design.

531
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:54,738
It detonates when the button
is pressed and then released.

532
00:26:54,822 --> 00:26:58,117
A bomb design like this
is all over the dark web.

533
00:26:58,200 --> 00:27:00,828
Which means it will be difficult
to identify a suspect.

534
00:27:01,829 --> 00:27:02,996
Anything on your end?

535
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:05,999
Right, we checked
all the security cameras in the building,

536
00:27:06,083 --> 00:27:08,961
but there's too much foot traffic,
and the cameras are too far away

537
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:10,337
to identify the suspect.

538
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:12,339
The account that sent the DM was fake too.

539
00:27:13,382 --> 00:27:14,758
I'm sure it was.

540
00:27:14,842 --> 00:27:16,885
No fingerprints were found on the device.

541
00:27:16,969 --> 00:27:19,972
Based on our analysis,
there wasn't much ammonium nitrate.

542
00:27:20,055 --> 00:27:23,267
Even if it had gone off, the blast radius
would've been about a meter.

543
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:28,814
In other words, it wasn't much of a bomb.
Right? Okay.

544
00:27:32,109 --> 00:27:34,903
If we hadn't defused it in time,
you would've lost your hands.

545
00:27:35,904 --> 00:27:38,031
Think before you start touching things.

546
00:27:42,119 --> 00:27:44,663
If I'd known it was a bomb,
I wouldn't have touched it.

547
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:45,998
Why didn't you know?

548
00:27:46,623 --> 00:27:47,958
You were given all the clues.

549
00:27:54,131 --> 00:27:55,215
What're you looking at?

550
00:27:57,426 --> 00:28:00,429
Ma'am, we came up
with a whole new concept.

551
00:28:00,512 --> 00:28:03,181
There's no need for that.
I'm not going to go on camera.

552
00:28:03,849 --> 00:28:05,267
Please delete everything you filmed today.

553
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:09,730
But if you were in it,
it'd help the police's image.

554
00:28:10,230 --> 00:28:11,690
I don't have time,

555
00:28:11,773 --> 00:28:14,067
and I don't want my face out there.

556
00:28:14,151 --> 00:28:15,527
Please delete the footage.

557
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:21,491
What do we do?

558
00:28:21,992 --> 00:28:23,994
We have nothing for next week's show.

559
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,330
I know.

560
00:28:27,623 --> 00:28:28,624
I said, I know.

561
00:28:29,082 --> 00:28:31,960
[sighs] This reminds me of that saying,

562
00:28:32,044 --> 00:28:34,963
"Better the devil you know." [sighs]

563
00:28:35,047 --> 00:28:36,924
The ship's sailed. Now you're in trouble.

564
00:28:37,007 --> 00:28:38,926
[clicking tongue] Bet you miss me now.

565
00:28:42,596 --> 00:28:43,597
What?

566
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:53,857
[door opens]

567
00:28:54,733 --> 00:28:55,734
[door closes]

568
00:28:58,987 --> 00:28:59,988
Hey, Joo.

569
00:29:01,323 --> 00:29:02,324
Sir.

570
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:03,659
It's been a while.

571
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:05,452
[chuckles] It has.

572
00:29:05,535 --> 00:29:06,578
Coffee?

573
00:29:07,788 --> 00:29:10,123
-[chuckles]
-How have you been?

574
00:29:10,207 --> 00:29:12,709
Oh. Same old, same old.

575
00:29:12,793 --> 00:29:14,628
I miss being out in the field.

576
00:29:15,837 --> 00:29:18,924
I heard you've been doing great
over there in SOU.

577
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:20,676
[chuckling]

578
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,636
-It's all thanks to you.
-So you do know.

579
00:29:22,719 --> 00:29:24,680
[both chuckle]

580
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:26,306
How does it feel to be back here?

581
00:29:27,683 --> 00:29:29,351
It really takes me back.

582
00:29:29,434 --> 00:29:31,061
Gangha is like home to me.

583
00:29:32,145 --> 00:29:33,397
Guess I'll be seeing you around.

584
00:29:33,981 --> 00:29:35,232
Yes.

585
00:29:35,315 --> 00:29:37,401
My team is going to work here for a while.

586
00:29:37,985 --> 00:29:40,112
Detective Jin Isoo needs protection too.

587
00:29:40,195 --> 00:29:42,656
Sure. Team 1 doesn't have
a leader right now,

588
00:29:42,739 --> 00:29:44,658
so I'll leave the case in your hands.

589
00:29:44,741 --> 00:29:45,742
All right.

590
00:29:46,785 --> 00:29:48,787
It might just be a prank,

591
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:51,081
but someone
could actually be after Jin Isoo.

592
00:29:51,164 --> 00:29:52,582
I know.

593
00:29:54,042 --> 00:29:56,128
You need to catch the suspect quickly.

594
00:29:56,962 --> 00:29:57,963
Got it.

595
00:30:04,177 --> 00:30:05,470
[sighs]

596
00:30:10,392 --> 00:30:12,519
Can I let go? Do I let go?

597
00:30:12,602 --> 00:30:13,895
[Kyungjin] Bro, run!

598
00:30:14,396 --> 00:30:15,689
[Hyera] Hey, nutjob.

599
00:30:15,772 --> 00:30:17,232
I told you to stay out of trouble.

600
00:30:17,315 --> 00:30:18,984
[♪ upbeat hip-hop music playing]

601
00:30:21,778 --> 00:30:22,863
Eyes forward.

602
00:30:24,114 --> 00:30:25,741
You're not crying, are you?

603
00:30:26,324 --> 00:30:27,576
[Isoo] That instructor from hell...

604
00:30:27,659 --> 00:30:29,036
[Kyungjin] It's her?

605
00:30:29,119 --> 00:30:30,454
Hey, nutjob!

606
00:30:30,537 --> 00:30:32,706
Think before you start touching things.

607
00:30:46,303 --> 00:30:47,471
[cell phone vibrates]

608
00:30:49,014 --> 00:30:51,850
[Hyeonwoo] Please forgive us
and answer your phone.

609
00:30:51,933 --> 00:30:53,560
[Jaeeun] We weren't thinking straight.

610
00:30:53,643 --> 00:30:54,811
[cell phone vibrating]

611
00:30:54,895 --> 00:30:57,481
SBC DIRECTOR KANG JAEEUN

612
00:30:57,564 --> 00:30:58,565
Jeez.

613
00:31:00,192 --> 00:31:02,944
[sighs] Why are you being so clingy? Huh?

614
00:31:05,781 --> 00:31:09,117
Well, I do have an event today
that would make for good content.

615
00:31:10,869 --> 00:31:13,622
Okay, fine. Then write up a new contract.

616
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:17,250
Nothing goes on air
until I've seen the final edit.

617
00:31:18,502 --> 00:31:20,378
Okay. Bye.

618
00:31:22,297 --> 00:31:23,298
[line disconnects]

619
00:31:26,343 --> 00:31:28,762
We're leading
this investigation as of today.

620
00:31:29,846 --> 00:31:31,264
We don't need any desks.

621
00:31:32,015 --> 00:31:33,517
We'll use the conference table.

622
00:31:40,732 --> 00:31:43,068
She thinks she's some big-shot
team leader, doesn't she?

623
00:31:44,361 --> 00:31:46,738
-I'm heading out first. Dress sharp.
-[Junyoung] Okay.

624
00:31:46,822 --> 00:31:48,782
Detective Jin, where are you going?

625
00:31:51,284 --> 00:31:53,411
I have a launch event today.

626
00:31:53,495 --> 00:31:56,081
-A launch event?
-For a whiskey I developed.

627
00:31:57,749 --> 00:31:59,626
Don't you know moonlighting's prohibited?

628
00:32:00,210 --> 00:32:03,004
I started it four years ago
but quit when I became a cop.

629
00:32:03,088 --> 00:32:04,256
Don't go.

630
00:32:05,006 --> 00:32:06,216
What?

631
00:32:06,299 --> 00:32:07,801
[♪ dramatic music playing]

632
00:32:08,343 --> 00:32:10,679
-But I'm the star of the event.
-Then push it back.

633
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:11,847
[scoffs]

634
00:32:13,598 --> 00:32:14,933
[sighs deeply]

635
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:19,062
Do I still look like
a recruit to you? Huh?

636
00:32:27,279 --> 00:32:28,280
Is that an order?

637
00:32:28,363 --> 00:32:31,533
I've been assigned to lead this case.
Didn't you get the memo?

638
00:32:32,534 --> 00:32:33,535
I did.

639
00:32:33,618 --> 00:32:35,871
We still haven't identified
a bombing suspect.

640
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:37,497
They might be after you.

641
00:32:38,290 --> 00:32:41,168
It's probably a prank.
They even gave us clues.

642
00:32:41,251 --> 00:32:43,336
It was just to humiliate me,

643
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:46,423
and it was a huge success thanks to you.

644
00:32:46,506 --> 00:32:48,800
Besides, I've always had
people out to kill me.

645
00:32:48,884 --> 00:32:49,926
Why?

646
00:32:50,010 --> 00:32:51,178
Just, you know,

647
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:53,305
for petty reasons.

648
00:32:55,182 --> 00:32:57,642
All the more reason to be careful.
Don't go.

649
00:32:58,852 --> 00:33:03,356
My security team
is checking every box, so just let it go.

650
00:33:04,524 --> 00:33:06,651
I'll handle it, okay?

651
00:33:07,986 --> 00:33:08,987
See you guys later.

652
00:33:09,905 --> 00:33:10,906
[sighs softly]

653
00:33:16,703 --> 00:33:17,954
-[door closes]
-[clears throat]

654
00:33:18,038 --> 00:33:19,039
We will

655
00:33:20,916 --> 00:33:22,334
keep an eye on him.

656
00:33:22,417 --> 00:33:23,460
Right.

657
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:25,253
We'll watch over him.

658
00:33:29,132 --> 00:33:30,300
-[sighs]
-[door closes]

659
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:38,225
[♪ elegant piano music playing]

660
00:33:58,411 --> 00:34:00,038
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

661
00:34:00,956 --> 00:34:02,332
[crowd cheering]

662
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:07,879
-Jin Isoo!
-Jin Isoo!

663
00:34:08,672 --> 00:34:10,840
-Jin Isoo!
-Jin Isoo!

664
00:34:25,397 --> 00:34:26,398
[in English] Cheers.

665
00:34:27,023 --> 00:34:28,775
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

666
00:34:32,988 --> 00:34:34,322
[exhales contentedly]

667
00:34:37,826 --> 00:34:38,827
Bang!

668
00:34:38,910 --> 00:34:39,995
[giggles]

669
00:34:43,456 --> 00:34:44,457
Oh?

670
00:34:45,208 --> 00:34:46,418
Kwaktube.

671
00:34:46,918 --> 00:34:48,795
[in Korean] I thought
you'd be too busy to come.

672
00:34:48,878 --> 00:34:50,463
-No way.
-You're looking good.

673
00:34:50,547 --> 00:34:52,090
Oh, come on.

674
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:53,258
By the way,

675
00:34:53,341 --> 00:34:54,718
isn't your wife due soon?

676
00:34:54,801 --> 00:34:56,177
She's actually due tomorrow.

677
00:34:56,261 --> 00:34:57,262
[gasps]

678
00:34:57,554 --> 00:34:58,638
[cell phone vibrating]

679
00:35:00,056 --> 00:35:01,933
-The hospital...
-The hospital?

680
00:35:02,767 --> 00:35:03,768
Hello?

681
00:35:04,519 --> 00:35:05,937
Yes. What?

682
00:35:07,439 --> 00:35:08,523
I need to go right now.

683
00:35:08,607 --> 00:35:09,774
Right now?

684
00:35:09,858 --> 00:35:10,859
The baby's coming.

685
00:35:10,942 --> 00:35:11,985
The baby...

686
00:35:14,154 --> 00:35:15,447
Good luck!

687
00:35:16,489 --> 00:35:18,783
[sighs] Hope the baby
doesn't take after the dad.

688
00:35:19,451 --> 00:35:21,119
Ah. I'm the one who made this.

689
00:35:21,202 --> 00:35:23,330
The logo is the defining feature,
you get...

690
00:35:23,872 --> 00:35:24,873
Hold on.

691
00:35:25,957 --> 00:35:27,792
[sighs] Clothes do make the man.

692
00:35:27,876 --> 00:35:28,877
What?

693
00:35:29,336 --> 00:35:31,087
[in English] Oh, oh. Stop.

694
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,050
[in Korean] What are you doing here?

695
00:35:35,133 --> 00:35:36,259
I didn't invite you.

696
00:35:36,843 --> 00:35:37,927
I'm going to check inside.

697
00:35:38,011 --> 00:35:40,639
There's no need. You're embarrassing me.

698
00:35:41,723 --> 00:35:43,600
You can't be here dressed like that.

699
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:45,352
Ever heard of a dress code?

700
00:35:46,186 --> 00:35:47,270
You two, head inside.

701
00:35:47,979 --> 00:35:48,980
Go.

702
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:50,815
Security.

703
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:54,944
Get her out of here, okay?
Dress code violation.

704
00:35:55,028 --> 00:35:56,279
-Hey, Jin Isoo.
-Let's go.

705
00:35:56,363 --> 00:35:58,281
Wait, Jin Isoo... [sighs]

706
00:36:00,158 --> 00:36:02,077
[exclaims] That damn nutjob.

707
00:36:12,712 --> 00:36:14,130
What happened?

708
00:36:14,214 --> 00:36:15,465
It's nothing.

709
00:36:24,057 --> 00:36:25,058
Keep watch.

710
00:36:25,141 --> 00:36:26,851
[♪ smooth jazz music playing]

711
00:36:34,442 --> 00:36:35,568
[Isoo] Mmm.

712
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,865
Oh, this smells great.

713
00:36:40,949 --> 00:36:44,202
Right? There's a subtle hint of vanilla.

714
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:45,328
Try it. Cheers.

715
00:36:45,412 --> 00:36:46,413
[glasses clink]

716
00:36:49,541 --> 00:36:51,751
I'll drink it later, just in case.

717
00:36:53,712 --> 00:36:55,630
Me too. We need to protect you.

718
00:36:56,381 --> 00:36:58,007
I told you, it's fine.

719
00:36:58,091 --> 00:37:00,301
I don't need protecting. [sighs]

720
00:37:05,223 --> 00:37:06,474
Oh...

721
00:37:06,558 --> 00:37:09,227
That's what your job does to you.
She can't switch off.

722
00:37:10,979 --> 00:37:11,980
[scoffs]

723
00:37:13,565 --> 00:37:15,066
[sighs] Whatever. Just ignore her.

724
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:23,408
See? I told you nothing would happen.

725
00:37:23,491 --> 00:37:26,453
You guys didn't get a taste,
so I'll send you a whole box.

726
00:37:26,536 --> 00:37:27,996
Awesome.

727
00:37:29,330 --> 00:37:30,373
[Jaeeun] Thanks for today.

728
00:37:31,082 --> 00:37:32,917
I'll call you after we're done editing.

729
00:37:33,501 --> 00:37:35,044
Make sure I look cool, okay?

730
00:37:35,628 --> 00:37:36,629
-Okay.
-Good.

731
00:37:41,551 --> 00:37:42,844
Oh, no.

732
00:37:43,428 --> 00:37:45,430
Guess you couldn't find the bomb.

733
00:37:46,681 --> 00:37:47,974
Have a drink before you go.

734
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:50,518
-No.
-[Isoo] Suit yourself.

735
00:37:51,102 --> 00:37:53,146
You're going home, right?
Where do you live?

736
00:37:53,229 --> 00:37:54,230
[scoffs]

737
00:37:55,899 --> 00:37:56,983
Noblesse.

738
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:59,068
Don't wander around. Go straight home.

739
00:37:59,152 --> 00:38:01,154
-[sighs in exasperation]
-[cell phone vibrates]

740
00:38:06,493 --> 00:38:09,245
[♪ ominous music playing]

741
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:14,584
[distorted voice] Detective Jin,
did you think the game was over?

742
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:15,668
Round 2.

743
00:38:25,220 --> 00:38:27,180
[♪ intense music playing]

744
00:38:33,061 --> 00:38:34,437
What on earth?

745
00:38:48,243 --> 00:38:49,536
[glass shattering]

746
00:38:55,083 --> 00:38:57,836
[Isoo breathing heavily]

747
00:38:58,795 --> 00:39:00,672
[Hyera whimpering]

748
00:39:03,383 --> 00:39:05,635
-Are you okay?
-Yeah. You?

749
00:39:06,678 --> 00:39:07,804
[Junyoung] Kyungjin, you okay?

750
00:39:08,805 --> 00:39:09,973
Yeah, I'm fine.

751
00:39:14,102 --> 00:39:15,645
[breathing heavily]

752
00:39:22,235 --> 00:39:23,987
[sighs]

753
00:39:29,826 --> 00:39:31,411
[indistinct conversation]

754
00:39:39,961 --> 00:39:41,754
[♪ tense music continues]

755
00:39:56,644 --> 00:39:58,688
-[sighs]
-[cell phone vibrates]

756
00:40:06,821 --> 00:40:09,407
[♪ ominous music playing]

757
00:40:09,991 --> 00:40:11,492
[distorted voice] Detective Jin,
you got lucky.

758
00:40:13,453 --> 00:40:15,204
[disembodied malicious laughter]

759
00:40:17,498 --> 00:40:21,085
[news anchor] Another homemade bomb attack
has occurred in the heart of Seoul.

760
00:40:21,169 --> 00:40:25,256
Once again, Detective Jin Isoo
was at the center of the attack,

761
00:40:25,340 --> 00:40:30,219
as the attack took place at a venue
where he was hosting an event.

762
00:40:30,303 --> 00:40:34,515
Police say the suspect's motive
remains unknown.

763
00:40:34,599 --> 00:40:36,893
[♪ music swells, fades]

764
00:40:38,978 --> 00:40:40,897
[Junyoung] Thank you for your cooperation.

765
00:40:45,318 --> 00:40:47,195
Did you get the full staff and guest list?

766
00:40:47,278 --> 00:40:48,947
Yes, they just faxed it over.

767
00:40:51,032 --> 00:40:52,325
And the list of YouTubers?

768
00:40:52,408 --> 00:40:53,785
They'll check and send it over.

769
00:40:53,868 --> 00:40:56,537
Check the security footage
and identify anyone suspicious.

770
00:40:56,621 --> 00:40:57,622
-Got it.
-[Junyoung] Got it.

771
00:41:02,961 --> 00:41:05,254
[sighs] It's out of the camera's view.

772
00:41:06,714 --> 00:41:08,800
-[Junyoung] Is this all the footage?
-Yes.

773
00:41:10,593 --> 00:41:14,013
I'll check around the building.
You chase the YouTubers for their footage.

774
00:41:14,097 --> 00:41:15,139
Got it.

775
00:41:19,852 --> 00:41:22,230
[distorted voice] Detective Jin.
Let the game begin.

776
00:41:22,313 --> 00:41:23,439
[glass shattering]

777
00:41:23,523 --> 00:41:24,732
I have a gift for you.

778
00:41:24,816 --> 00:41:26,234
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[device beeping]

779
00:41:26,317 --> 00:41:27,318
-Don't touch that!
-[Kyungjin] Bro!

780
00:41:27,402 --> 00:41:28,820
[distorted voice] Did you think
the game was over?

781
00:41:31,114 --> 00:41:32,365
Detective Jin, you got lucky.

782
00:41:32,448 --> 00:41:34,283
[tinkling]

783
00:41:37,328 --> 00:41:39,288
[high-pitched ringing swells]

784
00:41:41,833 --> 00:41:43,710
-[high-pitched ringing stops]
-[gasps, panting]

785
00:41:44,293 --> 00:41:45,670
Are you okay?

786
00:41:46,421 --> 00:41:48,631
[panting heavily]

787
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:52,510
So...

788
00:41:52,593 --> 00:41:55,555
Is someone trying to kill you?

789
00:41:59,684 --> 00:42:00,893
You should stop filming now.

790
00:42:01,602 --> 00:42:03,438
But we signed a contract.

791
00:42:05,231 --> 00:42:07,775
You are no longer allowed in this office.
Please leave.

792
00:42:09,277 --> 00:42:10,570
[breath trembles]

793
00:42:17,869 --> 00:42:19,203
Detective Jin, a word?

794
00:42:20,288 --> 00:42:22,165
[♪ tense music playing]

795
00:42:25,418 --> 00:42:28,046
Write up a list of people
who might want to kill you.

796
00:42:29,297 --> 00:42:33,342
I didn't mean that literally.
No one actually wants me dead.

797
00:42:33,426 --> 00:42:34,802
Doesn't matter how trivial.

798
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:36,429
Write down anyone who hates you

799
00:42:36,512 --> 00:42:38,306
or anyone you've hurt.

800
00:42:38,389 --> 00:42:39,599
Everyone you can think of.

801
00:42:40,266 --> 00:42:42,185
It doesn't take much to hold a grudge.

802
00:42:42,268 --> 00:42:43,311
[sighs]

803
00:42:50,276 --> 00:42:51,486
Jin Isoo.

804
00:42:52,695 --> 00:42:55,448
Using a homemade bomb
means they have nothing to lose.

805
00:42:56,115 --> 00:42:57,283
They don't care if they die.

806
00:42:59,660 --> 00:43:02,413
That's how determined they are
to kill you.

807
00:43:08,628 --> 00:43:11,297
A pager was used
in the Seongje bombing three years ago.

808
00:43:11,380 --> 00:43:12,673
That's right.

809
00:43:12,757 --> 00:43:15,051
Ask for the file.
He should be out of prison by now.

810
00:43:15,885 --> 00:43:17,095
Yes, ma'am.

811
00:43:17,929 --> 00:43:19,639
[Kyungjin] I got the footage
from the YouTubers.

812
00:43:20,431 --> 00:43:21,432
[mouse clicks]

813
00:43:21,516 --> 00:43:23,601
[♪ foreboding music playing]

814
00:43:24,435 --> 00:43:25,436
[keyboard clacks]

815
00:43:36,405 --> 00:43:38,199
He seems suspicious.

816
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:39,742
-Wait.
-[keyboard clacks]

817
00:43:51,587 --> 00:43:52,588
NOH JINSU, AGE 27

818
00:43:52,672 --> 00:43:55,091
-It's him. Noh Jinsu, age 27.
-Right.

819
00:43:55,174 --> 00:43:56,634
[keyboard clacking]

820
00:43:56,717 --> 00:43:59,095
IDENTITY SEARCH
NOH JINSU

821
00:44:05,268 --> 00:44:09,021
His father worked at Hansu Chemical
and left eight months ago.

822
00:44:09,105 --> 00:44:12,066
-What's his address?
-17-38 Yongpae-dong.

823
00:44:12,859 --> 00:44:14,110
-Let's go.
-[Kyungjin] Okay.

824
00:44:17,321 --> 00:44:20,825
[officer] I checked the Seongje bombing.
Park Gyeongtae has indeed been released.

825
00:44:22,201 --> 00:44:23,327
Let's go check him out.

826
00:44:23,411 --> 00:44:24,412
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

827
00:44:24,954 --> 00:44:27,331
We identified a suspicious waiter.

828
00:44:27,415 --> 00:44:29,792
We're going to see someone
who built a similar bomb.

829
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:31,586
We'll go check on the waiter.

830
00:44:31,669 --> 00:44:34,005
Okay. I'll send my team as backup.
Be careful.

831
00:44:34,088 --> 00:44:35,089
-Got it.
-Got it.

832
00:44:37,842 --> 00:44:39,010
[pen clicks]

833
00:44:40,928 --> 00:44:42,013
[pen clicks]

834
00:44:43,973 --> 00:44:45,016
[pen clicks]

835
00:44:46,225 --> 00:44:47,393
[pen clicks]

836
00:44:48,811 --> 00:44:51,522
I should've killed you on that day.

837
00:44:51,606 --> 00:44:52,773
Shut up!

838
00:44:52,857 --> 00:44:53,941
[both grunting]

839
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:56,986
I'll take away everything you have.

840
00:44:57,069 --> 00:44:58,237
[pen clicks]

841
00:44:58,738 --> 00:44:59,739
[Isoo] Never die.

842
00:45:03,576 --> 00:45:05,369
Live forever, haunted by regret.

843
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:07,455
-[pen clicks]
-[door opens]

844
00:45:09,498 --> 00:45:10,499
Mr. Choi.

845
00:45:14,212 --> 00:45:15,213
Are you all right?

846
00:45:16,380 --> 00:45:17,381
Not really.

847
00:45:20,593 --> 00:45:23,095
I've been told to find someone
who wants to kill me,

848
00:45:25,139 --> 00:45:26,849
but I can only think of one person

849
00:45:27,475 --> 00:45:29,227
who would want to kill me

850
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:32,230
and actually be capable of it.

851
00:45:34,982 --> 00:45:36,776
[♪ foreboding music playing]

852
00:45:42,990 --> 00:45:46,661
SPECIAL OPERATIONS UNIT

853
00:46:07,682 --> 00:46:09,892
[♪ foreboding music continues]

854
00:46:41,424 --> 00:46:42,550
[beaker clinks]

855
00:46:51,767 --> 00:46:53,102
Keep quiet and stand by.

856
00:46:55,980 --> 00:46:57,023
[loud knocking]

857
00:46:58,733 --> 00:46:59,942
You have a visitor.

858
00:47:06,449 --> 00:47:07,450
It's your brother,

859
00:47:08,117 --> 00:47:09,118
Jin Isoo.

860
00:47:10,119 --> 00:47:12,371
[♪ gentle melancholy music playing]

861
00:47:59,668 --> 00:48:00,795
[door opens]

862
00:48:02,254 --> 00:48:03,255
[door closes]

863
00:48:12,390 --> 00:48:13,391
[rattles, clatters]

864
00:48:13,474 --> 00:48:15,101
[♪ foreboding music playing]

865
00:48:16,268 --> 00:48:17,728
Park Gyeongtae, don't move.

866
00:48:24,151 --> 00:48:25,611
Turn around slowly.

867
00:48:37,832 --> 00:48:39,041
Noh Jinsu!

868
00:48:42,628 --> 00:48:43,671
What's all this?

869
00:48:43,754 --> 00:48:45,548
[♪ foreboding music continues]

870
00:49:00,104 --> 00:49:01,105
[gasps]

871
00:49:05,818 --> 00:49:07,862
-Who are you?
-Police.

872
00:49:09,572 --> 00:49:11,615
-[whirring]
-[Gyeongtae] That thing...

873
00:49:11,699 --> 00:49:12,950
It'll blow if we leave it.

874
00:49:15,911 --> 00:49:17,788
-[gun cocks]
-Don't move.

875
00:49:25,838 --> 00:49:27,673
-[dial clicks]
-[whirring stops]

876
00:49:30,926 --> 00:49:32,178
[sniffles]

877
00:49:33,012 --> 00:49:34,096
Is that your next bomb?

878
00:49:35,389 --> 00:49:36,390
No.

879
00:49:38,350 --> 00:49:41,395
It's fertilizer for the future of farming.

880
00:49:41,479 --> 00:49:43,063
Yes, fertilizer.

881
00:49:44,231 --> 00:49:45,816
But it's also used to make bombs.

882
00:49:46,567 --> 00:49:48,903
This is what caused
the explosion in Lebanon.

883
00:49:59,788 --> 00:50:00,998
You made this, didn't you?

884
00:50:05,628 --> 00:50:06,629
[Gyeongtae] Ah...

885
00:50:06,712 --> 00:50:08,255
Ah, that.

886
00:50:08,797 --> 00:50:11,300
It's been all over the Internet
for three years now.

887
00:50:12,218 --> 00:50:14,512
I've already served my time.

888
00:50:14,595 --> 00:50:16,138
I don't do that anymore.

889
00:50:17,431 --> 00:50:19,808
I set it off back then
because of that jerk I worked for.

890
00:50:19,892 --> 00:50:21,018
Lately,

891
00:50:22,436 --> 00:50:24,271
I've been using my brain for other things.

892
00:50:27,733 --> 00:50:29,568
INVENTION COMPETITION

893
00:50:29,652 --> 00:50:31,403
[♪ music swells, fades]

894
00:50:34,740 --> 00:50:35,741
AWARD CERTIFICATE

895
00:50:36,867 --> 00:50:37,868
[Jinsu] A bomb?

896
00:50:38,786 --> 00:50:41,413
[spluttering] It wasn't me.

897
00:50:43,082 --> 00:50:44,291
Then what were you doing?

898
00:50:47,920 --> 00:50:49,129
[exhales deeply]

899
00:50:49,838 --> 00:50:51,090
It's really nothing big.

900
00:50:51,173 --> 00:50:53,509
-You're Jin Isoo's stalker, right?
-Huh?

901
00:50:53,592 --> 00:50:55,511
Were you so obsessed
you wanted to kill him?

902
00:50:55,594 --> 00:50:56,887
We'll talk at the station.

903
00:50:57,680 --> 00:50:59,557
[spluttering]

904
00:51:01,350 --> 00:51:02,351
It's a talisman.

905
00:51:05,271 --> 00:51:06,272
What?

906
00:51:08,274 --> 00:51:09,650
It's a talisman.

907
00:51:11,402 --> 00:51:13,195
People still make bombs like this?

908
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:15,781
But it'll be tough to catch them.

909
00:51:18,117 --> 00:51:21,328
[chuckles] That's easy to make.

910
00:51:21,412 --> 00:51:24,665
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

911
00:51:27,042 --> 00:51:28,335
The shaman told me

912
00:51:29,753 --> 00:51:32,089
to leave it beside the person
I want to become,

913
00:51:32,172 --> 00:51:34,425
and then I'd receive divine revelation

914
00:51:34,508 --> 00:51:38,095
and make a lot of money like Jin Isoo.

915
00:51:38,178 --> 00:51:40,014
But then it actually blew up.

916
00:51:41,724 --> 00:51:42,725
Isn't that amazing?

917
00:51:46,186 --> 00:51:47,730
What was inside it?

918
00:51:49,940 --> 00:51:50,941
Well...

919
00:51:51,483 --> 00:51:53,319
My fingernails, some hair,

920
00:51:53,819 --> 00:51:54,945
and the paper talisman.

921
00:51:55,904 --> 00:51:59,408
Then why did your father leave his job?
Wasn't he forced to resign?

922
00:51:59,491 --> 00:52:00,492
My dad?

923
00:52:01,994 --> 00:52:04,163
He moved to the countryside
to take up farming.

924
00:52:05,247 --> 00:52:06,248
He grows persimmons.

925
00:52:15,299 --> 00:52:16,300
It's been a while.

926
00:52:17,426 --> 00:52:18,636
How have you been?

927
00:52:19,219 --> 00:52:21,555
[♪ gentle poignant music playing]

928
00:52:21,639 --> 00:52:23,223
I'm not here to check in on you.

929
00:52:24,850 --> 00:52:25,851
Right.

930
00:52:28,937 --> 00:52:30,356
Someone's trying to kill me.

931
00:52:32,941 --> 00:52:33,942
What?

932
00:52:39,490 --> 00:52:41,700
Someone's trying to kill me with a bomb.

933
00:52:41,784 --> 00:52:43,202
Who?

934
00:52:45,954 --> 00:52:46,955
Yeah.

935
00:52:48,832 --> 00:52:50,042
Who could it be?

936
00:52:51,502 --> 00:52:53,170
No matter how much I think about it,

937
00:52:55,172 --> 00:52:57,049
you're the only one I can think of.

938
00:53:10,854 --> 00:53:12,648
I have a lot of time here.

939
00:53:15,693 --> 00:53:16,694
So...

940
00:53:18,654 --> 00:53:22,074
I keep thinking
about what a fool I've been.

941
00:53:24,535 --> 00:53:25,703
I wrote you a letter.

942
00:53:26,537 --> 00:53:27,621
Several times.

943
00:53:29,665 --> 00:53:30,874
I made excuses

944
00:53:32,543 --> 00:53:33,919
and asked for forgiveness.

945
00:53:35,504 --> 00:53:37,256
But I couldn't bring myself to send it.

946
00:53:39,383 --> 00:53:41,385
Because I don't deserve to be forgiven.

947
00:53:44,304 --> 00:53:45,514
[sighs]

948
00:53:47,307 --> 00:53:48,308
Isoo.

949
00:53:51,270 --> 00:53:52,438
It's not me.

950
00:53:53,313 --> 00:53:54,898
My biggest regret

951
00:53:55,983 --> 00:53:57,109
is hurting you.

952
00:53:57,192 --> 00:53:58,235
Hurting me?

953
00:53:59,903 --> 00:54:00,946
[scoffs]

954
00:54:02,239 --> 00:54:03,240
No.

955
00:54:06,368 --> 00:54:08,454
You ruined my life.

956
00:54:17,880 --> 00:54:19,423
It probably isn't revenge.

957
00:54:24,261 --> 00:54:25,637
The Isoo I know...

958
00:54:28,599 --> 00:54:31,351
would never make someone
want revenge this badly.

959
00:54:32,603 --> 00:54:33,604
It might be...

960
00:54:35,647 --> 00:54:37,107
driven by desire.

961
00:54:44,239 --> 00:54:45,282
[door opens]

962
00:54:46,408 --> 00:54:47,493
[door slams]

963
00:54:48,243 --> 00:54:49,244
Isoo.

964
00:55:04,760 --> 00:55:06,094
[Mr. Choi] Will you be all right?

965
00:55:06,595 --> 00:55:08,931
I think you should go somewhere safe.

966
00:55:10,182 --> 00:55:11,308
I'll be fine.

967
00:55:11,808 --> 00:55:14,436
This is a police station.

968
00:55:14,520 --> 00:55:16,104
-[chuckles softly]
-[door opens]

969
00:55:20,192 --> 00:55:23,153
Call me if you need anything.

970
00:55:25,864 --> 00:55:26,865
Bye.

971
00:55:31,870 --> 00:55:34,164
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

972
00:55:39,836 --> 00:55:41,672
[♪ pensive music playing]

973
00:55:41,755 --> 00:55:43,257
TARGET BELIEVED TO BE JIN ISOO

974
00:55:44,007 --> 00:55:46,301
I put a surveillance team
on Park Gyeongtae.

975
00:55:46,385 --> 00:55:47,719
We're also tracing his bank accounts.

976
00:55:48,512 --> 00:55:52,391
So anyone can make that kind of bomb,
not just Park Gyeongtae?

977
00:55:52,975 --> 00:55:55,018
Yes. What about the waiter?

978
00:55:55,936 --> 00:55:57,437
He just idolizes Jin Isoo.

979
00:55:58,772 --> 00:55:59,773
[sighs]

980
00:56:03,569 --> 00:56:05,028
Where have you been?

981
00:56:06,071 --> 00:56:07,281
I had somewhere to go.

982
00:56:07,364 --> 00:56:08,532
Don't you get it?

983
00:56:10,284 --> 00:56:11,535
Someone's after you.

984
00:56:12,119 --> 00:56:13,537
I know.

985
00:56:16,582 --> 00:56:18,208
That's why I went to see him.

986
00:56:20,085 --> 00:56:22,004
The one person who wants to kill me.

987
00:56:22,671 --> 00:56:23,755
Who?

988
00:56:26,550 --> 00:56:27,551
My brother.

989
00:56:31,972 --> 00:56:32,973
He...

990
00:56:33,599 --> 00:56:35,684
[Hyera] I know. You don't need to explain.

991
00:56:40,564 --> 00:56:41,565
So?

992
00:56:43,025 --> 00:56:44,067
You think it's him?

993
00:56:45,986 --> 00:56:47,988
He's never had any visitors.

994
00:56:48,614 --> 00:56:50,532
He even refused to see his lawyer.

995
00:56:58,707 --> 00:57:01,293
We're still monitoring Park Gyeongtae,

996
00:57:01,376 --> 00:57:03,629
but we're unable to identify
a suspect at this point.

997
00:57:03,712 --> 00:57:05,380
-[sighs]
-For now, I think we should move

998
00:57:05,464 --> 00:57:07,090
Detective Jin to a safe house.

999
00:57:08,383 --> 00:57:10,052
-A safe house?
-Yes.

1000
00:57:10,969 --> 00:57:14,514
We'll take him to one of the safe houses
secured by the Counterterrorism Team.

1001
00:57:14,598 --> 00:57:15,599
Where is it?

1002
00:57:17,309 --> 00:57:19,770
Sorry, sir,
but I can't share that information.

1003
00:57:20,937 --> 00:57:22,022
What?

1004
00:57:22,105 --> 00:57:24,441
There could be someone
in the station with a grudge.

1005
00:57:25,609 --> 00:57:30,781
Are you saying
the culprit could be one of our own?

1006
00:57:30,864 --> 00:57:32,616
-Sir.
-[Hyera] It's just a precaution.

1007
00:57:33,992 --> 00:57:35,285
Just to be safe.

1008
00:57:35,786 --> 00:57:36,828
[exhales in disbelief]

1009
00:57:36,912 --> 00:57:39,414
All this trouble
just because of one rich kid.

1010
00:57:40,207 --> 00:57:42,793
Safe house or wherever,
just get him out of here.

1011
00:57:42,876 --> 00:57:44,836
-Before something goes wrong.
-Yes, sir.

1012
00:57:44,920 --> 00:57:47,589
Put Team 1 with him. You can trust them.

1013
00:57:48,298 --> 00:57:49,549
Yes, I'll do that.

1014
00:57:54,054 --> 00:57:56,640
Detective Jin Isoo,
you'll be moving to a safe house.

1015
00:57:56,723 --> 00:57:59,267
We're leaving now. Quietly.
Team 1 will join you.

1016
00:57:59,351 --> 00:58:00,977
Where exactly are we going?

1017
00:58:01,561 --> 00:58:02,854
I'll tell you on the way.

1018
00:58:02,938 --> 00:58:04,189
Give me a break.

1019
00:58:04,272 --> 00:58:06,608
I just need to stay holed up at home.
I'm not going.

1020
00:58:06,692 --> 00:58:09,528
We don't have a suspect,
and your place isn't safe either.

1021
00:58:10,112 --> 00:58:11,905
You're a target now.
You don't get to decide.

1022
00:58:15,200 --> 00:58:16,368
[sighs wearily]

1023
00:58:20,497 --> 00:58:21,498
[car alarm chirps]

1024
00:58:21,581 --> 00:58:22,666
Get in this one.

1025
00:58:23,166 --> 00:58:25,252
I can't just ride in any car. [scoffs]

1026
00:58:28,338 --> 00:58:30,966
You want to make it obvious
Jin Isoo is in that car?

1027
00:58:34,553 --> 00:58:35,554
Get in.

1028
00:58:37,389 --> 00:58:39,391
[muttering] Who does she think she is,
my boss?

1029
00:58:39,474 --> 00:58:40,684
Get in.

1030
00:59:03,915 --> 00:59:05,959
[♪ ominous music plays]

1031
00:59:13,258 --> 00:59:15,135
[Kyungjin] Maybe I should've gotten
in that car.

1032
00:59:15,218 --> 00:59:17,220
I don't think we should leave them alone.

1033
00:59:17,304 --> 00:59:19,306
I'm sure they won't fight.

1034
00:59:19,389 --> 00:59:20,640
They're not kids.

1035
00:59:23,393 --> 00:59:24,770
Nutjob, you asleep?

1036
00:59:28,106 --> 00:59:30,150
What do you want now?

1037
00:59:31,526 --> 00:59:32,611
There's no need to be scared.

1038
00:59:33,195 --> 00:59:34,446
Nothing bad will happen.

1039
00:59:35,197 --> 00:59:36,865
We'll catch them while you're there.

1040
00:59:36,948 --> 00:59:39,159
You think I'm an idiot or something?

1041
00:59:39,242 --> 00:59:40,243
I'm a cop too.

1042
00:59:41,578 --> 00:59:42,579
[chuckles softly]

1043
00:59:45,290 --> 00:59:46,958
Why are you even a cop?

1044
00:59:48,251 --> 00:59:49,628
Picking a fight with me again?

1045
00:59:49,711 --> 00:59:51,338
No, I'm just curious.

1046
00:59:51,421 --> 00:59:53,590
You're incredibly rich,

1047
00:59:53,673 --> 00:59:55,175
and you can do whatever you want.

1048
00:59:56,468 --> 00:59:57,761
Then what about you?

1049
00:59:57,844 --> 00:59:59,805
If you were incredibly rich,
would you quit?

1050
01:00:00,764 --> 01:00:02,599
-No.
-Same with me.

1051
01:00:02,682 --> 01:00:05,644
I've tried and done it all,
but this is my calling.

1052
01:00:06,561 --> 01:00:07,562
What?

1053
01:00:08,104 --> 01:00:09,564
Run out of fights to pick?

1054
01:00:12,609 --> 01:00:13,610
[scoffs]

1055
01:00:13,944 --> 01:00:15,320
You sure are different.

1056
01:00:16,696 --> 01:00:19,032
Says the person
who's been calling me a nutjob.

1057
01:00:19,115 --> 01:00:20,283
[vibrating]

1058
01:00:20,367 --> 01:00:21,451
Just answer your phone.

1059
01:00:24,079 --> 01:00:25,163
It's not me.

1060
01:00:26,164 --> 01:00:27,791
[vibrating continues]

1061
01:00:29,251 --> 01:00:30,252
It's not me either.

1062
01:00:33,171 --> 01:00:34,172
What's that?

1063
01:00:35,674 --> 01:00:38,051
It's a box I've never seen before.

1064
01:00:40,303 --> 01:00:41,888
What are you doing?

1065
01:00:42,764 --> 01:00:44,224
That red light on the box...

1066
01:00:44,307 --> 01:00:45,851
[vibrating continues]

1067
01:00:52,691 --> 01:00:53,942
[♪ ominous music playing]

1068
01:00:54,025 --> 01:00:55,485
[timer beeping]

1069
01:00:56,111 --> 01:00:57,696
-It's a bomb.
-What?

1070
01:00:58,280 --> 01:00:59,739
It's a bomb!

1071
01:01:00,657 --> 01:01:02,367
[tires screeching]

1072
01:01:02,450 --> 01:01:04,536
[♪ tense music playing]

1073
01:01:04,619 --> 01:01:06,621
[car horns blaring]

1074
01:01:15,255 --> 01:01:16,298
What's going on?

1075
01:01:16,381 --> 01:01:17,549
There's a bomb in the car.

1076
01:01:17,632 --> 01:01:19,634
Blast radius is 50... No, 100 meters.

1077
01:01:20,468 --> 01:01:21,595
Take the wheel.

1078
01:01:22,304 --> 01:01:24,014
[inhales sharply, mutters indistinctly]

1079
01:01:32,063 --> 01:01:33,565
[tires screeching]

1080
01:01:36,484 --> 01:01:37,819
Four minutes left.

1081
01:01:44,284 --> 01:01:45,493
[tires screech]

1082
01:01:47,871 --> 01:01:48,997
[exhales sharply]

1083
01:01:50,373 --> 01:01:51,708
-[timer beeping]
-[Isoo mutters indistinctly]

1084
01:01:53,793 --> 01:01:55,211
[engine revving]

1085
01:01:56,129 --> 01:01:57,130
GANGHA QUAY

1086
01:01:57,964 --> 01:01:59,299
I know a place.

1087
01:02:02,093 --> 01:02:03,261
[tires screeching]

1088
01:02:06,556 --> 01:02:07,849
-[car horn blares]
-[tires screech]

1089
01:02:10,685 --> 01:02:12,354
Wait, stop!

1090
01:02:12,437 --> 01:02:14,439
-[car horn honking]
-[siren blaring]

1091
01:02:20,570 --> 01:02:21,780
[tires screeching]

1092
01:02:34,084 --> 01:02:35,794
[♪ tense music playing]

1093
01:02:41,967 --> 01:02:43,301
[grunting]

1094
01:02:47,555 --> 01:02:48,556
[grunts]

1095
01:02:51,351 --> 01:02:52,936
[Hyera] There are people here. Be careful.

1096
01:02:54,896 --> 01:02:56,356
[car horn honking]

1097
01:02:58,191 --> 01:02:59,275
[grunts]

1098
01:03:00,527 --> 01:03:01,778
[car horn honking]

1099
01:03:05,115 --> 01:03:06,574
[tires screeching]

1100
01:03:07,283 --> 01:03:08,576
Detective Park, stop!

1101
01:03:08,660 --> 01:03:09,661
[tires screech]

1102
01:03:09,744 --> 01:03:11,871
[siren blaring distantly]

1103
01:03:24,217 --> 01:03:25,301
[tires screech]

1104
01:03:28,388 --> 01:03:30,140
-Nine seconds.
-Open the door.

1105
01:03:31,016 --> 01:03:32,434
-What?
-Open the door!

1106
01:03:42,235 --> 01:03:43,570
[suspenseful music intensifies]

1107
01:03:55,290 --> 01:03:56,624
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 1

1108
01:03:56,708 --> 01:03:57,917
SERIAL BOMBING ATTACKS BEGIN...
WHO IS AFTER JIN ISOO?

1109
01:03:58,001 --> 01:04:01,421
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1110
01:04:22,525 --> 01:04:25,945
Special Cast.
Kwak Siyang, Kwaktube, Bae Seongjae

1111
01:04:33,036 --> 01:04:34,454
-[cell phone vibrates]
-[distorted voice] Come alone.

1112
01:04:34,537 --> 01:04:36,414
He'll blow up if I see anyone else.

1113
01:04:36,498 --> 01:04:38,291
-[Isoo] Mr. Choi!
-[Hyeonwoo] I got a DM.

1114
01:04:38,374 --> 01:04:40,794
-I was told to come here and film you die.
-Detective!

1115
01:04:40,877 --> 01:04:43,171
-[Hyera] I think Jin Isoo has been set up.
-[explosion]

1116
01:04:43,254 --> 01:04:45,090
I don't know how far ahead they planned.

1117
01:04:45,173 --> 01:04:47,717
Whose idea was it
to do a feature on Detective Jin Isoo?

1118
01:04:47,801 --> 01:04:49,219
[in English] Action.

1119
01:04:49,302 --> 01:04:51,304
[Isoo, in Korean] I think I know
what the bombers are after.

1120
01:04:51,387 --> 01:04:53,473
-[Kyungjin] Isoo disappeared.
-Detective Jin!

1121
01:04:53,556 --> 01:04:54,557
We need a different location.

1122
01:04:54,641 --> 01:04:56,768
-Is this Joo Hyera's place?
-The bomber would never expect it.

1123
01:04:56,851 --> 01:04:59,145
I didn't expect it either.
I'm going to a hotel.

1124
01:04:59,229 --> 01:05:00,230
Once Jin Isoo leaves,

1125
01:05:00,313 --> 01:05:02,190
I'd like to pick his replacement.

1126
01:05:02,273 --> 01:05:03,817
[Isoo] No way. Is someone...

1127
01:05:03,900 --> 01:05:06,945
[Hyera] It sent Jin Isoo to a safe house
and isolated him.

1128
01:05:07,695 --> 01:05:09,572
[Isoo] That bastard was bluffing.

1129
01:05:11,699 --> 01:05:13,451
[narrator, on TV] Next week's Specialist

1130
01:05:13,535 --> 01:05:17,247
is a third-generation billionaire heir
and violent crimes detective,

1131
01:05:17,330 --> 01:05:18,873
Senior Inspector Jin Isoo.

1132
01:05:18,957 --> 01:05:22,502
He recently arrested members
of a pyramid scheme ring in Mexico.

1133
01:05:23,002 --> 01:05:26,422
Detective Jin joined the police through
a special recruitment program for lawyers

1134
01:05:26,506 --> 01:05:29,509
-and has since built an impressive career.
-[sighs] That nutjob.

1135
01:05:29,592 --> 01:05:33,346
Don't miss next week's episode
on Flex Cop Senior Inspector Jin Isoo.

1136
01:05:38,852 --> 01:05:40,854
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
